WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.410
- Bed time is the safest,
coziest, warmest time of all.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.310
- Hi I am Noel MacNeal,

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.513
I am a puppeteer, yes, it's a weird word.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.440
This happened back in 1997

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.650
so I actually went in that morning

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.120
to audition for another character

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.470
for a game show that they
were trying to develop.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.420
I got a call from Henson
saying please come back

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.600
'cause we want you to audition
for this other character.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.370
I went in and I put on
what's called the helix,

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.860
it's like the understructure
with the hoop rings

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.060
and the netting and this
foam head and then I realized

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.280
wait a minute it is quarter
to five, this is a courtesy,

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.650
you're not gonna get this, so I just said

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.360
forget it you know what
I'm just gonna have fun.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.970
Come Monday around six o'clock,
just shy of six o'clock,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.890
that's when I got the call
saying Noel you got the part

00:00:58.890 --> 00:00:59.723
and I was like what?

00:00:59.723 --> 00:01:02.843
And it's like yep, so
that's how it happened.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.253
When you're inside

00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:11.370
you put your right arm up through
the neck and into the head

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.840
and you put your hand inside the mouth

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.500
so that the lower thumb is his
lower jaw and this is up here

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.810
and it was like a little trigger
for me to do his eyebrows.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.760
Then my left hand was in his left arm

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.840
and there was a tiny little
string, a monofilament

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.460
that went up to a little ring in his neck

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:32.030
that came down the other side

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.720
to the right hand which was stuffed

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.270
so whenever I moved this hand

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.280
this one would move automatically

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.810
especially when he was dancing.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.570
Give a guess, how hot was it inside?

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.900
I just put in a little
thermometer one time

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.010
so it got up to like about 92 degrees

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.470
but it's dry heat and the season,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.620
especially the first season,

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.720
they would crank up the air
conditioning in the studio

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.150
so it would be freezing

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.390
and people would always complain about it

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.120
but it had to offset the fact

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.730
that the guy in the
bear suit might pass out

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.130
so they'd just crank up
the air conditioning.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:07.933
- Hmm? It's you!

00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:09.850
Ooh.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.110
- Mitchell Kriegman who created the show

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.760
just had it so that Bear would
just like sniff the camera.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.593
I came up with

00:02:16.593 --> 00:02:19.260
him really jamming it in
and pulling it back out

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.110
which kids always reacted to

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:26.110
in fact one message I got
was from a mom of a kid

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:29.030
who was severely handicapped

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:32.360
and had not really responded
even by the age of two

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.090
and she was watching
the show and as soon as

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.330
Bear like jammed his nose
into the camera to sniff,

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.260
that's when she jumped back
and it was the first time

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.980
she had actually reacted
to the outside world

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.130
and they were thrilled
beyond measure so yeah,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.290
sniffing can benefit the world.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.680
I've been getting lots of
fan email from the parents

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.970
and from the kids of
autism and special needs

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.080
who've grown up with Bear

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.400
and how they said it's
still comforting for them

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.000
and I realized today
there's no show like that

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.340
where it's just sincere, it's just gentle,

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.390
and it's just as comforting as
Bear was, it's not too loud,

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.390
it's not in your face,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.000
well except for when he sniffs the camera.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.970
So then I've been trying
to develop my show

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.230
called the Show Me Show

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.300
for kids with autism and special needs

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.630
to kinda fill that niche

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.640
'cause I know for a fact that
the kid networks right now

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.123
aren't gonna do that, so.

